[ti:Banks and Their Customers]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.43]Lesson 12 | 第12课
[00:02.26]Banks and their customers | 银行和顾客
[00:07.92]Why is there no risk to the customer when a bank prints the customer's name on his cheques? | 当银行把顾客的名字印在支票上时，为什么顾客不会有风险？
[00:15.50]When anyone opens a current account at a bank, he is lending the bank money, | 任何人在银行开活期账户时，他就是把钱借给了银行，
[00:20.69]repayment of which he may demand at any time either in cash or by drawing a cheque in favour of another person. | 这笔钱他可以随时提取，或者用现金，或者开一张付款给别人的支票。
[00:29.28]Primarily, the banker-customer relationship is that of debtor and creditor-- | 首先，银行与顾客的关系是债务人和债权人的关系——
[00:35.26]who is which depending on whether the customer's account is in credit or is overdrawn. | 究竟谁是债务人谁是债权人，要看顾客的账户是有结余还是透支。
[00:40.53]But, in addition to that basically simple concept, | 但是，除了这个基本上简单的概念之外，
[00:43.76]the bank and its customer owe a large number of obligations to one another. | 银行和顾客彼此之间还负有许多义务。
[00:49.72]Many of these obligations can give rise to problems and complications but a bank customer, unlike, say, a buyer of goods, | 这些义务中有许多会引起问题和纠纷，但是一位银行顾客，比如说，不像购买商品的顾客，
[00:58.87]cannot complain that the law is loaded against him. | 不能抱怨法律对他不利。
[01:02.59]The bank must obey its customer's instructions, and not those of anyone else. | 银行必须遵照顾客的指示行事，而不是别人的指示。
[01:07.79]When, for example, a customer first opens an account, he instructs the bank to debit his account only in respect of cheques drawn by himself. | 例如，顾客第一次开户时，就指示银行只凭他本人签发的支票记入他账户的借方。
[01:17.88]He gives the bank specimens of his signature, and there is a very firm rule | 他把签名的样本交给银行，而且有一条非常严格的规则：
[01:22.82]that the bank has no right or authority to pay out a customer's money on a cheque | 银行没有任何权利或权限凭一张支票动用顾客的钱款，
[01:27.94]on which its customer's signature has been forged. | 如果那张支票上顾客的签名是伪造的。
[01:31.90]It makes no difference that the forgery may have been a very skillful one: | 伪造得再巧妙也无济于事：
[01:36.48]the bank must recognize its customer's signature. | 银行必须能够识别顾客的签名。
[01:40.24]For this reason there is no risk to the customer in the practice, adopted by banks, of printing the customer's name on his cheques. | 因此，银行把顾客的名字印在他的支票上这一做法，对顾客没有风险。
[01:49.00]If this facilitates forgery, it is the bank which will lose, not the customer. | 如果这种做法方便了伪造，遭损失的将是银行，而不是顾客。
